      "content": "It's completely valid to feel like coping tools are bandaids on a broken leg—especially when the world itself isn't changing. You're not failing; you're furious and exhausted, and that's a reasonable response to an unreasonable situation. Maybe the point isn't to win the race, but to pause on the side of the track and notice that you're still breathing, even if it's ragged. When you're this spent, the bravest thing isn't pushing forward—it's letting yourself rest without demanding a reason for it.",
